{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"primary","scenes":[{"caption":"Sharing in a ratio","duration_ms":9000,"id":"s1","narration":"Two children share forty-eight dollars in the ratio two to three. We split the money into two plus three — five equal parts.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"q","kind":"text","size":44,"text":"$48 shared in the ratio 2 : 3","x":120,"y":90}},{"at_ms":600,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#7fb3e8","h":56,"id":"barA","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":176,"x":120,"y":160}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#8fd694","h":56,"id":"barB","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":264,"x":120,"y":248}},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cutA","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":208,"x2":208,"y1":160,"y2":216}},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cutB1","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":208,"x2":208,"y1":248,"y2":304}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cutB2","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":296,"x2":296,"y1":248,"y2":304}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labA","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"2 parts — child A","x":520,"y":200}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labB","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"3 parts — child B","x":520,"y":288}},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"whole","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"whole = 2 + 3 = 5 parts","x":520,"y":380}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"emphasize","dur_ms":1000,"target":"whole"},{"at_ms":6400,"do":"caption","text":"First ask: how many equal parts?"}]},{"caption":"Watch out: 3:2 is not 3/2 of the whole","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s2","narration":"Careful: a ratio of two to three does not mean two over three of the money. The whole is five parts, so three parts is three fifths.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"q","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"Is 3 parts = 3/2 of the whole?","x":120,"y":140}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#8a1f1f","id":"warn","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"No. 3 : 2 means 3 parts out of 5 — not 3 out of 2.","x":120,"y":205}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#ffffff","h":60,"id":"bar","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":440,"x":120,"y":280}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"c1","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":208,"x2":208,"y1":280,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"c2","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":296,"x2":296,"y1":280,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":3600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"c3","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":384,"x2":384,"y1":280,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":3800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"c4","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3,"x1":472,"x2":472,"y1":280,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":4400,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#8fd694","h":60,"id":"three","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":264,"x":120,"y":280}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"frac","kind":"text","size":38,"text":"3 parts out of 5 = 3/5 of the whole","x":120,"y":420}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#8a1f1f","id":"bad","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"3/2 × $48 = $72 ≠ $48 — impossible!","x":120,"y":480}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"caption","text":"The whole is always the sum of the parts"}]},{"caption":"One part, then multiply","duration_ms":10000,"id":"s3","narration":"Five equal parts share forty-eight dollars. One part is forty-eight divided by five: nine dollars sixty. Then two parts and three parts are easy.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"q","kind":"text","size":44,"text":"1 part = $48 ÷ 5","x":120,"y":90}},{"at_ms":700,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#ffffff","h":56,"id":"barA","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":176,"x":120,"y":160}},{"at_ms":1300,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#8fd694","h":56,"id":"barB","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":264,"x":120,"y":248}},{"at_ms":1900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"onepart","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"1 part = $48 ÷ 5 = $9.60","x":520,"y":200}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"shareA","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"A: 2 × $9.60 = $19.20","x":520,"y":290}},{"at_ms":4100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"shareB","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"B: 3 × $9.60 = $28.80","x":520,"y":380}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"check","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"check: $19.20 + $28.80 = $48.00","x":120,"y":448}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"emphasize","dur_ms":1000,"target":"check"},{"at_ms":7000,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"ans","kind":"text","size":40,"text":"A gets $19.20, B gets $28.80 ✓","x":120,"y":505}},{"at_ms":8400,"do":"caption","text":"Divide first, then multiply by the parts"}]},{"caption":"The takeaway","duration_ms":6000,"id":"s4","narration":"To share in a ratio, add the parts to find the whole, divide to find one part, then multiply for each share.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"t1","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"1. Add the parts: 2 + 3 = 5 parts in the whole","x":120,"y":200}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"t2","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"2. Divide: $48 ÷ 5 = $9.60 per part","x":120,"y":260}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"t3","kind":"text","size":40,"text":"3. Multiply by the parts:","x":120,"y":350}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"t4","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"2 × $9.60 = $19.20, 3 × $9.60 = $28.80 ✓","x":120,"y":410}}]}],"subject":"math","title":"Ratio: sharing $48 in 2:3","topic":"ratio"}